# Squares of a Sorted Array — LeetCode 977

**Pattern:** Two Pointers  
**Approach:** Compare absolute values from both ends

## Approach
1. Initialize `low = 0`, `high = n - 1`.
2. Create an answer array of size `n`.
3. Traverse the answer array from right to left.
4. Compare `Math.abs(nums[low])` and `Math.abs(nums[high])`.
5. Place the larger square at `ans[i]` and move its pointer inward.
6. Return `ans`.

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {
    public int[] sortedSquares(int[] nums) {
        int low = 0;
        int high = nums.length - 1;
        int[] ans = new int[nums.length];

        for (int i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (Math.abs(nums[low]) > Math.abs(nums[high])) {
                ans[i] = nums[low] * nums[low];
                low++;
            } else {
                ans[i] = nums[high] * nums[high];
                high--;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
